/E (ENGINEERING DECISION 1: The centralized single-owner state management architecture is selected and defended. By restricting state write permissions to exactly one deterministic thread running at high RTOS priority, race conditions are mathematically eliminated. The state representation is guaranteed to be temporally and semantically consistent at all times. Furthermore, the centralized engine enables atomic multi-event evaluation, provides an isolated audit point for CENELEC EN 50128 formal verification, and allows safe state rollbacks if an actuator task reports a hardware failure during command execution. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
