/T (In operational railway environments, external events occurasynchronously and frequently arrive in close temporal proximity. For example, an automated train approach signal may arrive precisely as a road vehicle stalls on the crossing, while an operator turns a manual override key and a sensor self-test flags a parity error. Without a mathematically rigorous priority hierarchy and deterministic conflict-resolution engine, simultaneous events can cause priority inversion, missed deadlines,or contradictory actuator commands. )
