/T (Event Ordering: Events arriving within the same RTOSschedulingtick \(1 ms\) are sorted in the queue strictly by their priority tier rather than arrivalorder.ATier1emergency event posted 100 microseconds after a Tier 4 telemetry packet is immediatelyinsertedat the head of the queue. Event Loss & Queue Starvation: The event queueisstaticallypre-allocated with a depth of 16 descriptors. If an extreme burst threatens queue overflow,thequeuemanager implements Priority- Based Tail-Drop: incoming Tier 4 events are rejectedandcountedina drop counter, while Tier 1 and Tier 2 events are guaranteed storage. )
