/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (ENGINEERING DECISION 2: To prevent contradictory actuator commands, a Hardware-Interlocked Actuator Token Architecture is designed. Actuator driver tasks \(Barrier Motor Control, Warning Lights, Sirens\) never accept commands directly from functional detection tasks. Instead, they only accept an Actuator Execution Token issued exclusively by the Central State Machine Manager. Furthermore, barrier motor direction is protected by a Hardware Mutex and an interlocked relay bridge: the UP and DOWN H- bridge gate drivers share a hardware break-before-make lockout circuit that physically prevents simultaneous activation even in the event of software corruption. If a manual override command requests 'OPEN' while the state machine is in S2, S3, S4, or S5, the command is rejected by an immutable Safety Assertion Guard, and an unauthorized override violation event is dispatched to the critical event log. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
