<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (malloc/free\) for event records. In safety-critical embedded systems,dynamic heap allocation introduces three fatal risks: \(1\) Heap fragmentation over extended operation,leading to sudden allocation failure; \(2\) Non-deterministic execution latency in memory management routines;and \(3\) Catastrophic system lockup during high-frequency event bursts when heap exhaustion occurs.)
/E (malloc/free\) for event records. In safety-critical embedded systems,dynamic heap allocation introduces three fatal risks: \(1\) Heap fragmentation over extended operation,leading to sudden allocation failure; \(2\) Non-deterministic execution latency in memory management routines;and \(3\) Catastrophic system lockup during high-frequency event bursts when heap exhaustion occurs.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
