659 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (The logging subsystem is re-engineered with an entirelystatic, bounded dual-ring architecture divided into two physically isolated buffers operating withoutdynamic heap allocation. )
/E (The logging subsystem is re-engineered with an entirelystatic, bounded dual-ring architecture divided into two physically isolated buffers operating withoutdynamic heap allocation. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
660 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (Critical Safety Buffer \(Ring 0\): Pre-allocated in non-volatileFerroelectric RAM \(FRAM\). Capacity = 128 slots x 32 bytes = 4,096 bytes. Dedicated exclusivelytoTier 1 and Tier 2 events \(emergency stops, sensor failures, barrier collisions, FSM state changes\). Ring 0 NEVER overwrites uncommitted records. If buffer occupancy reaches 90%, ahigh-priority flush alarm is signaled to telemetry, and the system transitions to a protected degradedstate rather than losing a safety record. Informational Buffer \(Ring 1\): Pre-allocated in static systemSRAM. Capacity = 512 slots x 32 bytes = 16,384 bytes. Dedicated to Tier 3 and Tier 4 events\(telemetry heartbeats, routine sensor readings, operator logins\). Operates as a high-throughputcircular FIFO where the oldest informational records are overwritten when full. )
/E (Critical Safety Buffer \(Ring 0\): Pre-allocated in non-volatileFerroelectric RAM \(FRAM\). Capacity = 128 slots x 32 bytes = 4,096 bytes. Dedicated exclusivelytoTier 1 and Tier 2 events \(emergency stops, sensor failures, barrier collisions, FSM state changes\). Ring 0 NEVER overwrites uncommitted records. If buffer occupancy reaches 90%, ahigh-priority flush alarm is signaled to telemetry, and the system transitions to a protected degradedstate rather than losing a safety record. Informational Buffer \(Ring 1\): Pre-allocated in static systemSRAM. Capacity = 512 slots x 32 bytes = 16,384 bytes. Dedicated to Tier 3 and Tier 4 events\(telemetry heartbeats, routine sensor readings, operator logins\). Operates as a high-throughputcircular FIFO where the oldest informational records are overwritten when full. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
