/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (FINAL ENGINEERING DECISION: DEPLOYMENT IS UNEQUIVOCALLY RECOMMENDED \(DECISION: YES\). The finalized RTOS-based railway crossing architecture resolves every operational deficiency observed during field testing. By replacing uncoordinated multi-task state modification with a deterministic, centralized 9-state Mealy FSM, eliminating dynamic heap allocation in favor of static zero- heap dual-ring buffers, guaranteeing hard real-time scheduling margins via SRP and task slicing, and providing a robust, interlocked manual-override and degraded-mode safety net, the architecture establishes absolute functional safety. The design fully complies with international railway safety standards \(CENELEC EN 50126, EN 50128, and IEC 61508 SIL-4\) and is formally cleared for commercial field deployment. )
/E (FINAL ENGINEERING DECISION: DEPLOYMENT IS UNEQUIVOCALLY RECOMMENDED \(DECISION: YES\). The finalized RTOS-based railway crossing architecture resolves every operational deficiency observed during field testing. By replacing uncoordinated multi-task state modification with a deterministic, centralized 9-state Mealy FSM, eliminating dynamic heap allocation in favor of static zero- heap dual-ring buffers, guaranteeing hard real-time scheduling margins via SRP and task slicing, and providing a robust, interlocked manual-override and degraded-mode safety net, the architecture establishes absolute functional safety. The design fully complies with international railway safety standards \(CENELEC EN 50126, EN 50128, and IEC 61508 SIL-4\) and is formally cleared for commercial field deployment. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
733 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (adopts an extended conservative timing profile: \(a\) Pre-warning visual/acoustic duration is increased from 5.0 s to 8.0 s to provide ample escape time for road users; \(b\) Barrier motor descent speed is reduced by 25% to allow visual pedestrian escape; \(c\) A Tier 1 incident packet is dispatched to telemetry; and \(d\) An automated wireless speed-restriction beacon is transmitted to approaching rolling stock, limiting train approach velocity to 25 km/h. 5. Automated Self-Healing and Recovery: If the sensor restores communication and generates continuous valid self-test frames for at least 10 consecutive seconds, Task T6 is re-enabled in a staging mode. Full automated authority is restored ONLY when the crossing transitions to S0 \(Normal\), preventing abrupt control mode shifts while a train is present. )
/E (adopts an extended conservative timing profile: \(a\) Pre-warning visual/acoustic duration is increased from 5.0 s to 8.0 s to provide ample escape time for road users; \(b\) Barrier motor descent speed is reduced by 25% to allow visual pedestrian escape; \(c\) A Tier 1 incident packet is dispatched to telemetry; and \(d\) An automated wireless speed-restriction beacon is transmitted to approaching rolling stock, limiting train approach velocity to 25 km/h. 5. Automated Self-Healing and Recovery: If the sensor restores communication and generates continuous valid self-test frames for at least 10 consecutive seconds, Task T6 is re-enabled in a staging mode. Full automated authority is restored ONLY when the crossing transitions to S0 \(Normal\), preventing abrupt control mode shifts while a train is present. )
