/Title (FINAL ENGINEERING DECISION: DEPLOYMENT IS UNEQUIVOCALLY RECOMMENDED \(DECISION: YES\). The finalized RTOS-based railway crossing architecture resolves every operational deficiency observed during field testing. By replacing uncoordinated multi-task state modification with a deterministic, centralized 9-state Mealy FSM, eliminating dynamic heap allocation in favor of static zero- heap dual-ring buffers, guaranteeing hard real-time scheduling margins via SRP and task slicing, and providing a robust, interlocked manual-override and degraded-mode safety net, the architecture establishes absolute functional safety. The design fully complies with international railway safety standards \(CENELEC EN 50126, EN 50128, and IEC 61508 SIL-4\) and is formally cleared for commercial field deployment.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 813 0 R
/Next 959 0 R
>>
endobj
959 0 obj
