/Title (Scenario:During active service, the Doppler radar / optical grid road-vehicle obstacle sensor suffers a completehardware failure or power disconnection, while railway track sensors and barrier actuators continueoperating normally. A naive system might either stall the crossing indefinitely \(causing gridlock\) or operateblindly \(risking trapping vehicles\). Our architecture implements a mathematically defensible, multi-faceted Degraded-Mode Policy.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1283 0 R
/Next 1377 0 R
>>
endobj
1368 0 obj
<<
/Title (adopts an extended conservative timing profile: \(a\) Pre-warning visual/acoustic duration is increased from 5.0 s to 8.0 s to provide ample escape time for road users; \(b\) Barrier motor descent speed is reduced by 25% to allow visual pedestrian escape; \(c\) A Tier 1 incident packet is dispatched to telemetry; and \(d\) An automated wireless speed-restriction beacon is transmitted to approaching rolling stock, limiting train approach velocity to 25 km/h. 5. Automated Self-Healing and Recovery: If the sensor restores communication and generates continuous valid self-test frames for at least 10 consecutive seconds, Task T6 is re-enabled in a staging mode. Full automated authority is restored ONLY when the crossing transitions to S0 \(Normal\), preventing abrupt control mode shifts while a train is present.)
/Dest [28 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1283 0 R
/Prev 1378 0 R
>>
endobj
