/Title (ENGINEERING CHALLENGE RESOLUTION: A catastrophic hazard arises if a new train approach event is processed using an outdated crossing state \(for example, assuming the barrier is down when it is actively opening\). To prevent this, the architecture implements a Monotonic Sequence Epoch Counter within a Stack Resource Policy \(SRP\) protected Crossing Status Block. Whenever a state transition occurs, the Epoch Counter increments atomically. When Task T2 validates a train approach, it stamps the event with the current Epoch ID. When Task T1 retrieves the event from the queue, it compares the stamped Epoch with the live Epoch. If an intervening transition occurred \(e.g., an emergency manual override\), the event is re- evaluated against the live state before any actuator command is issued, guaranteeing 100% state consistency.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1437 0 R
/Next 1454 0 R
>>
endobj
